# Build context is this folder (parent) so Dockerfiles can COPY the skill/bot.
# Keep the context tiny: ignore everything except the folders the images need.
*
!hermes-local
!hermes-skills
!assess-bot
!cassandra-bot
!colt_auth.py
!user_store.py
!webapp
# THE SECURITY BRAIN. webapp/Dockerfile does `COPY perseus /opt/perseus/perseus` because
# perseus.service runs `docker exec colt-web ... /opt/perseus/perseus/hub.py`, and that path only
# ever existed on the HOST. This file starts with `*`, so it is an ALLOW-LIST: a path that is not
# named here is excluded from the build context and the COPY fails with "/perseus: not found".
# Adding it to deploy_web_direct.INCLUDE was necessary and not sufficient - defect class 35 lists
# `.dockerignore` by name as the wiring point that gets missed, and it got missed.
!perseus
# ...but NOT the operator's node_modules. `COPY webapp/frontend/ ./` runs AFTER `npm install` in the
# fe stage, so a host node_modules would be copied straight OVER the fresh install — and npm
# packages carry PER-PLATFORM binaries (esbuild ships @esbuild/<os>-<arch> as an optional dep).
# The image would then be built with whatever platform the operator's folder happens to hold, which
# is exactly the class of failure that broke the i18n gate. Let the image install its own.
# dist/ and ssrtmp/ are build output; shipping them into the context only makes it bigger.
webapp/frontend/node_modules
webapp/frontend/dist
webapp/frontend/ssrtmp
